  "question": {
    "text": "A $12 \\mathrm{~V}$ battery connected to a coil of resistance $6 \\Omega$ through a switch, drives a constant current in the circuit. The switch is opened in $1 \\mathrm{~ms}$. The emf induced across the coil is $20 \\mathrm{~V}$. The inductance of the coil is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qrMp8",
      "text": "$5 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uFzDk",
      "text": "$12 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HrPZT",
      "text": "$8 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jYyYf",
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Induced emf, $\\varepsilon=-\\mathrm{L} \\frac{\\mathrm{dI}}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\Rightarrow 20=-\\mathrm{L} \\frac{(0-2)}{10^{-3}}$ Hence, inductance of the coil.<br />$\\mathrm{L}=10 \\mathrm{mH}$",
    "image": null
  },
